Z||000021||Taijiguy||07-12-2000||08:40 AM||||Steve you and I need to talk, I'm in the process of de-injecting my 2.8 right now. It's actually been simpler than I thought, and I'm working with an extremely tight budget. I can give you the skinny on the parts I had to replace and what they came from, and what the increase in performance seems to be. My desktop dyno indicates removing the fuel injection will be a good move. (no, I didn't base my decision to do it based on THAT!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I kept the cam I had before, whcih was too wild to keep the MAP sensor happy, I picked up an Edelbrock 4bbl setup, and will fabricate an adaptor to install two 70's Holley/Webber 5200 series carbs, or for the short term anyway, a Holley 390 4bbl.<BR>The great part is, that I sold off most of my no-longer-needed components, which helped to subsidize the project. Email me if you want to discuss this some more.<P>taiji||||reg||1
